  "lineage": "Yoruba were music: pre-dawn Ramadan-procession devotional song-and-drumming tradition of southwestern Nigerian Muslim-Yoruba communities, performed by ajiwere groups moving through Muslim neighborhoods before the suhoor pre-dawn meal during Ramadan. Performance combines unison or call-and-response chorus singing in Yoruba and Arabic (Quranic phrases interpolated into Yoruba praise-poetry) with sákárà frame-drums and small bells. Direct ancestor of fuji music — Alhaji Ayinde Barrister brought the were aesthetic into post-Ramadan secular commercial performance contexts.",
